    <section class="cg-section cg-about" id="how-it-works">
      <div class="cg-section-copy">
        <span class="cg-section-label">UNDERSTANDING CODE PLAGIARISM</span>
        <h2>What is programming code plagiarism?</h2>
        <p>
          Code plagiarism occurs when someone copies or reuses another
          person's program without appropriate acknowledgment. It can
          include copied logic, similar code structures, or reused
          implementations presented as original work.
        </p>
        <p>
          CodeGuard helps analyze submitted programs and highlight
          potential similarities so that students and educators can
          review the results more carefully.
        </p>
      </div>

